>Walker</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changing physicians' behavior: what works and thoughts on getting more things to work</article-title><source>J Contin Educ Health Prof</source><year>2002</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>243</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12613059</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/chp.1340220408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hawe</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Shiell</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Riley</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Complex interventions: how "out of control" can a randomised controlled trial be?</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2004</year><volume>328</volume><fpage>1561</fpage><lpage>1563</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15217878</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.328.7455.1561</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hammermeister</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Shroyer</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Sethi</surname><given-names>GK</given-names></name><name><surname>Grover</surname><given-names>FL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Why it is important to demonstrate linkages between outcomes of care and processes and structures of care</article-title><source>Med Care</source><year>1995</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>OS5</fpage><lpage>OS16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7475412</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rubenstein</surname><given-names>LV</given-names></name><name><surname>Pugh</surname><given-names>J</given-names>